
; FujiNet MS-DOS drivers
;
; FUJI_PORT  - COM port: 1-4 - Uses default hardcoded address & irq, OR
;                        Hex I/O address, followed by irq (e.g. FUJI_PORT=0x2f8,11)
;              Default: 1 (COM1)
;              The 1-4 COM numbering is PC-only; on other machines use the
;              hex form to name the serial chip's register address.
; FUJI_BPS   - Baud rate (9600, 19200, 115200, etc.)
;              Default: 115200 on the PC, 9600 on every other machine
; NOTIME     - Do not set DOS clock from FujiNet
;
; Non-PC machines load their own build of the driver instead of
; FUJINET.SYS - see the README. For example, on a Sanyo MBC-550:
;
;   DEVICE=FNSANYO.SYS

DEVICE=FUJINET.SYS FUJI_PORT=1 FUJI_BPS=115200
DEVICE=FUJIPRN.SYS 
